From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 10:15:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] rtworkq: Release completed serial work items

Regular serial work items retain one reference while they are linked in the
serial queue's pending list and another for the threadpool finalization
callback.  The worker releases its dispatch reference, but the finalizer only
released one of its two retained references after removing the item from the
pending list.  This leaked the async result, its callback, and users such as a
Media Foundation Source Reader and its private work queue.

Release both the pending-list and finalizer references once finalization is
complete.  Reply-mode items do not install this finalizer and are unaffected.

Reported and verified by atty303:
https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/715
---
 dlls/rtworkq/queue.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dlls/rtworkq/queue.c b/dlls/rtworkq/queue.c
--- a/dlls/rtworkq/queue.c
+++ b/dlls/rtworkq/queue.c
@@ -462,6 +462,7 @@ static void CALLBACK serial_queue_finalization_callback(PTP_CALLBACK_INSTANCE in
     LeaveCriticalSection(&queue->cs);
 
     IUnknown_Release(&item->IUnknown_iface);
+    IUnknown_Release(&item->IUnknown_iface);
 }
 
 static HRESULT serial_queue_init(const struct queue_desc *desc, struct queue *queue)
